				<headline type="str">Winter Weather Advisory issued November 26 at 1:40AM CST until November 26 at 12:00PM CST by NWS Paducah KY</headline>
				<description type="str">Our first winter storm of the season continues into Thanksgiving
morning. A sharp gradient between very little snow and impactful snow
amounts exists with additional snowfall occurring early this morning.

* WHAT...Wet snow. Additional snow accumulations between 1 to 2
inches.

* WHERE...Alexander, Jackson, Perry IL, and Union Counties.

* WHEN...Until noon CST today.

* IMPACTS...Plan on slippery road conditions. The hazardous
conditions will impact the Thursday morning commute.</description>
				<instruction type="str">Slow down and use caution while traveling. The latest road conditions
can be obtained by visiting www.weather.gov/pah/roads</instruction>
